From: =?UTF-8?q?Lajosh=C3=A1zi=2C=20L=C3=A1szl=C3=B3=20Gergely?=
 <lajoshazilg@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 05:01:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 102/104] ipa: simple: Allow the exposure time and the gain to
 be set
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The simple IPA computes both and offers no way to say otherwise, so an
application cannot hold a shutter speed, cannot pick a gain to keep noise
down, and cannot bracket an exposure. Implement ExposureTimeMode and
AnalogueGainMode with their manual values, as control_ids_core.yaml describes
them: a value sent while the quantity is automatic is dropped, and the
metadata reports which source each came from.

The two are independent, which is the point of there being two modes. With the
exposure time held and the gain automatic, a darkening scene has to be
answered with gain; with the gain held, with a longer exposure. The AGC's
ladder is therefore gated per quantity rather than skipped as a whole, so the
half that is still automatic keeps working and does the whole job.

Publishing a range for these controls needs the sensor's limits before the
camera is ever configured, since the ControlInfoMap an application sees is
built once at init() time. The limits are read there from the sensor's V4L2
controls, alongside the lens, and noted as a range for a user interface rather
than a promise: they can move when the sensor is reconfigured for another
resolution, so a value is clamped to the session's limits when it is applied.

Signed-off-by: Lajosházi, László Gergely <lajoshazilg@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
